{
  "note": [
    "Operator-supplied facts, used ONLY for fields the gateway did not report.",
    "Aleph prefers /model/info, which reports a gateway's own modes, windows and",
    "rates. That endpoint is admin-only, so an application virtual key usually",
    "sees just /v1/models (ids and nothing else). These entries fill that gap.",
    "",
    "CAPABILITY fields (mode, max_input_tokens, supports_*) are properties of the",
    "MODEL and are safe to state here.",
    "",
    "RATE fields are properties of YOUR DEPLOYMENT. Those below are publisher",
    "list prices in USD per token and are an ESTIMATE \u2014 verify against a bill.",
    "They are recorded as pricing_source=\"static\", never \"gateway\", so an",
    "auditor can tell asserted numbers from reported ones.",
    "",
    "Self-hosted / open-weight models are deliberately left UNPRICED: their cost",
    "depends on your infrastructure, and a guess would be recorded as fact. A",
    "bound model with no rate records pricing_source=\"unknown\" and logs an error,",
    "which is the intended, visible outcome. Fill in your own numbers below.",
    "",
    "Keys may be an exact model id or a 'prefix*' pattern; longest match wins.",
    "Override this whole file with ALEPH_MODEL_HINTS_PATH."
  ],
